IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-arrest`
IMPORT `ccc20-tests-fixtures`

-- ccc20-tests-arrest.l4 -- tests for ccc20-part16-arrest.l4 (ss 494 to 499). Expected values are hand-written from the text of lines 11074-11143.

§ `Tests -- section 494(1): any one may arrest without warrant`

-- args: offence, finds the person committing it, believes on reasonable grounds the person has committed a criminal offence, believes escaping and freshly pursued
-- (a) a person he finds committing an indictable offence (an offence that is both counts, unless the prosecutor elected summary conviction: s 493.01)
#ASSERT `s 494(1) any one may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture indictable` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 494(1) any one may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture hybrid` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 494(1) any one may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture hybrid elected` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 494(1) any one may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture summary` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 494(1) any one may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture indictable` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) a person who, on reasonable grounds, he believes (i) has committed a criminal offence and (ii) is escaping from and freshly pursued by persons with lawful authority to arrest
#ASSERT `s 494(1) any one may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture summary` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 494(1) any one may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture summary` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 494(1) any one may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture summary` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 494(2): the owner of property`

-- args: owner/possessor/authorized person, finds the person committing a criminal offence on or in relation to the property, arrest at that time, within a reasonable time, believes not feasible for a peace officer
#ASSERT `s 494(2) the owner of property, or a person acting for the owner, may arrest the person without a warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 494(2) the owner of property, or a person acting for the owner, may arrest the person without a warrant` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 494(2) the owner of property, or a person acting for the owner, may arrest the person without a warrant` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 494(2) the owner of property, or a person acting for the owner, may arrest the person without a warrant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 494(2) the owner of property, or a person acting for the owner, may arrest the person without a warrant` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 494(2) the owner of property, or a person acting for the owner, may arrest the person without a warrant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 494(3) and (4)`

-- args: the arrester is a peace officer, the arrest was made without warrant
#ASSERT `s 494(3) the arrester must forthwith deliver the person to a peace officer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 494(3) the arrester must forthwith deliver the person to a peace officer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 494(3) the arrester must forthwith deliver the person to a peace officer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the duty as a regulative rule: delivered, then FULFILLED; the case where the duty does not arise is FULFILLED outright (a trace prints the outcome; a DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT on the stable binary)
#TRACE `s 494(3) the delivery duty` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 494(3) the person who arrested without warrant, other than a peace officer` DOES `s 494(3) deliver the person to a peace officer` AT 1
#TRACE `s 494(3) the delivery duty` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
#TRACE `s 494(3) the delivery duty` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
-- (4) authorized under section 494 means authorized by law for section 25; anything else is not covered
#ASSERT `s 494(4) the person is authorized by law to make the arrest for the purposes of section 25` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 494(4) the person is authorized by law to make the arrest for the purposes of section 25` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 495(1): a peace officer may arrest without warrant`

-- args: offence, has committed it or the officer believes on reasonable grounds that the person has committed or is about to commit it, finds the person committing a criminal offence, believes a warrant is in force within the territorial jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 495(1) the peace officer may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture indictable` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(1) the peace officer may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture hybrid` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(1) the peace officer may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture summary` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 495(1) the peace officer may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture hybrid elected` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 495(1) the peace officer may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture summary` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(1) the peace officer may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture summary` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(1) the peace officer may arrest the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture indictable` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 495(2): the bar on arrest without warrant`

-- the three needs the text names in (d)(i) to (iii), and one it does not name ("including")
#ASSERT `s 495(2)(d) the circumstance is a need the text names` `s 495(2)(d)(i) the need to establish the identity of the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(2)(d) the circumstance is a need the text names` `s 495(2)(d)(ii) the need to secure or preserve evidence of or relating to the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(2)(d) the circumstance is a need the text names` `s 495(2)(d)(iii) the need to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(2)(d) the circumstance is a need the text names` `s 495(2)(d) a circumstance the text does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: class of offence, s 553 mention, (d) public interest may be satisfied without arrest, (e) no reasonable grounds to believe the person will fail to attend
#ASSERT `s 495(2) the peace officer is barred from arresting the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture class indictable` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(2) the peace officer is barred from arresting the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture class indictable` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 495(2) the peace officer is barred from arresting the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture class indictable` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 495(2) the peace officer is barred from arresting the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture class indictable` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 495(2) the peace officer is barred from arresting the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture class indictable` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 495(2) the peace officer is barred from arresting the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture class hybrid` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(2) the peace officer is barred from arresting the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture class hybrid` NOTHING FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 495(2) the peace officer is barred from arresting the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture class summary` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(2) the peace officer is barred from arresting the person without warrant` `s 493.01 fixture class summary` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 495(3): the consequences of arrest without warrant`

-- args: acting under (1), proceedings under an Act of Parliament, it is alleged and established that the officer did not comply with (2)
#ASSERT `s 495(3) the peace officer is deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of their duty` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 495(3) the peace officer is deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of their duty` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495(3) the peace officer is deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of their duty` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 495(3) the peace officer is deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of their duty` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- section 495.1`

#ASSERT `s 495.1 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant to take them before a judge or justice under section 524` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495.1 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant to take them before a judge or justice under section 524` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495.1 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant to take them before a judge or justice under section 524` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 495.1 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant to take them before a judge or justice under section 524` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- sections 496 and 497: appearance notices`

#ASSERT `s 496 the peace officer may, without laying a charge, issue an appearance notice to attend a judicial referral hearing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 496 the peace officer may, without laying a charge, issue an appearance notice to attend a judicial referral hearing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 496 the peace officer may, without laying a charge, issue an appearance notice to attend a judicial referral hearing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 497 args: the answer of s 495(2), class of offence, s 553 mention
#ASSERT `s 497 the peace officer may issue an appearance notice to the person` (JUST TRUE) `s 493.01 fixture class hybrid` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 497 the peace officer may issue an appearance notice to the person` (JUST TRUE) `s 493.01 fixture class summary` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 497 the peace officer may issue an appearance notice to the person` (JUST TRUE) `s 493.01 fixture class indictable` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 497 the peace officer may issue an appearance notice to the person` (JUST TRUE) `s 493.01 fixture class indictable` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 497 the peace officer may issue an appearance notice to the person` (JUST TRUE) `s 493.01 fixture class indictable` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 497 the peace officer may issue an appearance notice to the person` (JUST FALSE) `s 493.01 fixture class hybrid` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 497 the peace officer may issue an appearance notice to the person` NOTHING `s 493.01 fixture class hybrid` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 498(1), (1.01), (1.1), (2) and (3): release from custody after arrest without warrant`

-- args: arrested without warrant (or delivered or placed in custody: (1.01)), s 469 listing, already taken before a justice or released, how, offence described in 503(3)
#ASSERT `s 498(1) a peace officer must, as soon as practicable, release the person, subject to subsection (1.1)` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `s 498(1)(a) the peace officer intends to compel the person's appearance by way of summons` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(1) a peace officer must, as soon as practicable, release the person, subject to subsection (1.1)` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `s 498(1)(b) the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(1) a peace officer must, as soon as practicable, release the person, subject to subsection (1.1)` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `s 498(1)(c) the person gives an undertaking to the peace officer` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(1) a peace officer must, as soon as practicable, release the person, subject to subsection (1.1)` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `s 498(1) none of those three` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 498(1) a peace officer must, as soon as practicable, release the person, subject to subsection (1.1)` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE `s 498(1)(b) the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 498(1) a peace officer must, as soon as practicable, release the person, subject to subsection (1.1)` TRUE NOTHING FALSE `s 498(1)(b) the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 498(1) a peace officer must, as soon as practicable, release the person, subject to subsection (1.1)` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE `s 498(1)(b) the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 498(1) a peace officer must, as soon as practicable, release the person, subject to subsection (1.1)` FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `s 498(1)(b) the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 498(1) a peace officer must, as soon as practicable, release the person, subject to subsection (1.1)` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `s 498(1)(b) the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the four needs of (1.1)(a)(i) to (iv), and one the text does not name
#ASSERT `s 498(1.1)(a) the circumstance is a need the text names` `s 498(1.1)(a)(i) the need to establish the identity of the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(1.1)(a) the circumstance is a need the text names` `s 498(1.1)(a)(ii) the need to secure or preserve evidence of or relating to the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(1.1)(a) the circumstance is a need the text names` `s 498(1.1)(a)(iii) the need to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(1.1)(a) the circumstance is a need the text names` `s 498(1.1)(a)(iv) the need to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(1.1)(a) the circumstance is a need the text names` `s 498(1.1)(a) a circumstance the text does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1.1): the officer must not release if (a) public interest belief or (b) belief the person will fail to attend court
#ASSERT `s 498(1.1) the peace officer must not release the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(1.1) the peace officer must not release the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(1.1) the peace officer must not release the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the release duty as a regulative rule: release (FULFILLED); the duty displaced by (1.1) or not arising (FULFILLED outright)
#TRACE `s 498(1) the release duty` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 498(1) release the person` AT 3
#TRACE `s 498(1) the release duty` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
#TRACE `s 498(1) the release duty` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
-- (3) args: the officer arrested/held and did not release as described, proceedings under an Act of Parliament, alleged and established non-compliance with (1)
#ASSERT `s 498(3) the peace officer is deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of the officer's duty` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 498(3) the peace officer is deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of the officer's duty` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 498(3) the peace officer is deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of the officer's duty` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 498(3) the peace officer is deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of the officer's duty` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

